import SwiftUI
import KwipMLCore

enum PrebuiltModelsLessonContent {
    static let objective="This canvas groups synthetic customers by similar behavior. Table Input supplies an identifier and three numeric features. Prebuilt models fits K-means; its Assignments and Profiles flow to ordinary View tools. Save model preserves a frozen prepared-input model for later assignment.\n\nThis example is segmentation, not churn prediction. There is no historical churn outcome here, so no cluster can honestly be called a churn probability."
    static let terms="- **Feature:** one measured input per customer. Usage, recency and breadth in this fixture are comparable synthetic scores.\n- **Cluster:** a group of similar rows; its numeric ID has no inherent rank or business meaning.\n- **Centroid:** the fitted center of a cluster in feature coordinates.\n- **Silhouette:** a separation diagnostic, not accuracy or business value. Coverage and noise handling are explicit.\n- **Prepared input:** the exact ordered numeric features expected by a saved model; external preprocessing is not automatically packaged."
    static let steps=[
        "Select [Synthetic customer behavior](kwip-node://data/customers). Inspect the source table. Each row is one invented customer; customer_id is identity, not a feature. Usage, recency and breadth are synthetic comparable scores. [Declare numeric features](kwip-node://data/numeric) uses Columns to convert their CSV text into explicit float64 values, retaining customer_id as text. With real data, resolve missing values and fit any scaling/encoding only on the intended Training population.",
        "Select [Find behavior segments](kwip-node://control/segments), then Configure model. Task is Clustering, operation Fit population and algorithm K-means. In Data mapping, keep usage, recency and breadth in that order. Target is Not used. Apply saves settings; Run Flow performs fitting.",
        "Run Flow, then open [Inspect every assignment](kwip-node://data/assignments). Every input row and identity is retained. Cluster is an arbitrary group label. Distances measure proximity in these feature coordinates; they are not probabilities. Compare similar and dissimilar customers rather than naming an arbitrary cluster good or bad.",
        "Open [Compare segment profiles](kwip-node://data/profiles). Compare counts and feature means, including any noise group for DBSCAN. Component Metrics reports actual populations and sampled silhouette coverage. A 2D view cannot summarize every model feature; do not read diagnostic samples as the fitting population.",
        "Select [Save prepared-input model](kwip-node://control/save), choose Portable package and an unused destination, then save. Load model → Prebuilt / document model package can import its inert state. Configure a second Prebuilt models operation as Assign new rows, using the same algorithm/options and exact feature order. Apply the same frozen upstream preparation; do not refit a scaler on the new rows. DBSCAN has no predictive Model output, so disconnect model consumers before switching to that fit-only analysis.",
        "For supervised work, start a separate canvas: Table Input → Partition → Prebuilt models, with matching Training/Validation connections. Choose Classification or Regression, explicit ordered features and a separate target. Validate on held-out outcomes. Save/reload and Predict preserve that target's trained model, while Predict itself needs no labels. Review mistakes and leakage before making a useful-quality claim.\n\nThis segmentation canvas has no learned Preprocess chain. On a separate canvas with supported Training-fitted Preprocess steps, Save model can offer Model + learned preparation after fitting. Reload that package, connect its saved rules to Preprocess → Apply saved rules, then send the prepared table and loaded model to Predict. Keep earlier file typing and fixed cleanup explicit; never refit on the new rows."
    ]
    static let boundary="This editable practice is unscored. CPU-only reviewed built-in algorithms, bounded complete tables and safe prepared-input inference packages. No automatic churn labels, calibrated risk claim, arbitrary sklearn class loading, online partial-fit, GPU or optimizer continuation. Existing document TF-IDF and numeric/Keras projects retain their original contracts inside Prebuilt models."
}
struct PrebuiltModelsLearningView:View {
    @ObservedObject var store:WorkspaceStore
    var body:some View {Button("Open segmentation practice"){_=store.loadComponentWorkflowExample(PrebuiltModelsPractice.lessonID,device:"cpu")}.buttonStyle(FlatButtonStyle()).disabled(store.isBusy)}
}
